            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your 78-year-old female patient, admitted on 27/01/2022 due to an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. Pulse oximetry was monitored continuously throughout her stay. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators (salbutamol and ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. She responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided prior to discharge. Please ensure close outpatient follow-up and review of her maintenance inhaler regimen. Discharge diagnosis: COPD with acute exacerbation (ICD-10: J44.1).</div>
               </text>
            </section>
